"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">Ω</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≈</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.5806em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.03588em;\">ω</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3011em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">0</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>","key":"NCwoTZQfSz"},{"type":"text","value":"\nund können die Resonanzfrequenz numerisch bestimmen.","position":{"start":{"line":29,"column":1},"end":{"line":29,"column":1}},"key":"UmpAeHL3xQ"}],"key":"bCK7CBEz4q"}],"checked":false,"key":"d2yUmXyfW7"}],"key":"JVLhWl9YKW"}],"class":"attention","key":"kEo45XgdhZ"}],"key":"PPcQF8DIfp"},{"type":"block","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":35,"column":1},"end":{"line":35,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Gedämpfter Schwinger: die drei Fälle","position":{"start":{"line":35,"column":1},"end":{"line":35,"column":1}},"key":"iLM9ZBMoLm"}],"identifier":"ged-mpfter-schwinger-die-drei-f-lle","label":"Gedämpfter Schwinger: die drei Fälle","html_id":"ged-mpfter-schwinger-die-drei-f-lle","implicit":true,"key":"J6OypxCTQk"},{"type":"comment","value":" TODO: Unterabschnitt 1 (~10 min)\n     - Gedämpfte DGL: m*x_ddot + c*x_dot + k*x = 0\n     - Substitution wie in 11.1, aber f gibt jetzt [x_dot, (-k*x - c*x_dot)/m] zurück\n     - Dämpfungszahl D = c/(2*sqrt(k*m)) einführen, kritische Dämpfung c_krit = 2*sqrt(k*m)\n     - Kurvenschar x(t) für D in [0.2, 0.5, 1.0, 2.0], gleiche Anfangsbedingung x0=0.05 m\n     - Phasenporträt: Spiralen statt Ellipsen\n     - Rhetorische Frage kursiv: Welches D würden Sie für Ihren Pkw wählen? ","key":"PdQm0Lcdq4"}],"key":"NLajXXgN7E"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-code","children":[{"type":"code","lang":"python","executable":true,"value":"import numpy as np\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nimport matplotlib.style as style\nfrom scipy.integrate import solve_ivp\nstyle.use('seaborn-v0_8')\n\n# --- Parameter ---\nm       = 250.0\nk_feder = 16000.0\nomega_0 = np.sqrt(k_feder / m)    # = 8.0 rad/s\nc_krit  = 2 * np.sqrt(k_feder * m)   # kritische Dämpfung in N*s/m\nprint(f\"omega_0 = {omega_0:.2f} rad/s\")\nprint(f\"c_krit  = {c_krit:.1f} N*s/m\")\n\n# --- Rechte Seite: gedämpfter Schwinger ---\ndef f_gedaempft(t, y, c):\n    # y[0] = x (Position), y[1] = x_dot (Geschwindigkeit)\n    # m*x_ddot + c*x_dot + k*x = 0\n    # TODO: x_ddot = (-k*y[0] - c*y[1]) / m\n    x_dot  = y[1]\n    x_ddot = None   # TODO\n    return [x_dot, x_ddot]\n\n# TODO: Kurvenschar für D in [0.2, 0.5, 1.0, 2.0] plotten\n# Hinweis: c = D * c_krit, dann solve_ivp mit lambda t, y: f_gedaempft(t, y, c)\n# TODO: Phasenporträt (sol.y[0] vs. sol.y[1]) für alle vier D-Werte","key":"scuQjnXhbm"},{"type":"outputs","id":"4BwqU1PEtcxaaO-oPjRXO","children":[{"type":"output","children":[],"jupyter_data":{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":"omega_0 = 8.00 rad/s\nc_krit  = 4000.0 N*s/m\n"},"key":"SRHncCLkEG"}],"key":"iIHBXpb3Fs"}],"key":"JFCFqGFci9"},{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"comment","value":" TODO: Prosatext (~80 Wörter):\n     Erklärung der drei Fälle anhand der Plot-Ausgabe.\n     Formel für gedämpfte Eigenfrequenz: omega_d = omega_0 * sqrt(1 - D^2)\n     (nur für D < 1 reell). Warum D=1 die kürzeste Einschwingzeit hat.\n     Hinweis auf das Phasenporträt: einwärts spiralisierend statt Ellipse. ","key":"SXOBrTvtI9"},{"type":"admonition","children":[{"type":"admonitionTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mini-Übung","position":{"start":{"line":80,"column":1},"end":{"line":80,"column":1}},"key":"AJ46pDcKEa"}],"key":"oP92tXVjIh"},{"type":"comment","value":" TODO: Mini-Übung (5 min):\n     1. Berechnen Sie c für D = 0.3 von Hand (c = D * c_krit).\n     2. Verständnisfrage: Für D = 1.5 schwingt das System nicht. Wie erkennen\n        Sie das im Phasenporträt?\n     3. Nach wie vielen Sekunden ist |x| < 0.001 m für D = 0.2 vs. D = 1.0?\n        Schätzen Sie aus dem Plot ab. ","key":"HALpfdW2mI"}],"class":"tip","key":"ooBKqhVuQh"}],"key":"Xd0AoiJYeD"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-code","children":[{"type":"code","lang":"python","executable":true,"value":"# Code-Zelle","key":"Gk5Di9N5D3"},{"type":"outputs","id":"b1ZWlo8MCmHj6Q-jRb32J","children":[],"key":"zffdkTiK8r"}],"key":"EkQGJOFRd9"},{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"admonition","children":[{"type":"admonitionTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lösung","position":{"start":{"line":94,"column":1},"end":{"line":94,"column":1}},"key":"M18x5J4XcE"}],"key":"V7ppt8sPxr"},{"type":"comment","value":" TODO: Lösung zur Mini-Übung.\n     c_krit = 2*sqrt(16000*250) = 4000 N*s/m\n     D=0.3: c = 0.3 * 4000 = 1200 N*s/m\n     Phasenporträt D>1: monoton in Ursprung, keine Spirale (kein Vorzeichen-\n     wechsel von x_dot). ","key":"n5BrmXmLRA"}],"class":"tip dropdown","key":"katJ7PacBZ"}],"key":"yPtVpTGlNX"},{"type":"block","position":{"start":{"line":104,"column":1},"end":{"line":104,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":106,"column":1},"end":{"line":106,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Erzwungene Schwingung und Resonanz","position":{"start":{"line":106,"column":1},"end":{"line":106,"column":1}},"key":"htmwfsUzqh"}],"identifier":"erzwungene-schwingung-und-resonanz","label":"Erzwungene Schwingung und Resonanz","html_id":"erzwungene-schwingung-und-resonanz","implicit":true,"key":"v7KjSpsFR0"},{"type":"comment","value":" TODO: Unterabschnitt 2 (~10 min)\n     - Erzwungene DGL: m*x_ddot + c*x_dot + k*x = F0*sin(Omega*t)\n     - f gibt jetzt [x_dot, (-k*x - c*x_dot + F0*sin(Omega*t))/m] zurück\n     - Nichtautonom (Omega*t in f → t wird gebraucht)\n     - Zwei Phasen: Einschwingvorgang (Transient) + stationärer Zustand\n     - Stationäre Amplitude: A = max(|x|) im letzten Drittel der Simulation\n     - Resonanz bei Omega ≈ omega_0: Amplitudenmaximum zeigen\n     - Parameter: F0 = 500 N, D = 0.2, Omega variabel ","key":"RedW6FYegq"}],"key":"Boxx8FoLBj"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-code","children":[{"type":"code","lang":"python","executable":true,"value":"import numpy as np\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nimport matplotlib.style as style\nfrom scipy.integrate import solve_ivp\nstyle.use('seaborn-v0_8')\n\nm       = 250.0\nk_feder = 16000.0\nomega_0 = np.sqrt(k_feder / m)\nc_krit  = 2 * np.sqrt(k_feder * m)\nD       = 0.2\nc       = D * c_krit\nF0      = 500.0    # Kraftamplitude in N\n\n# --- Erzwungener Schwinger (nichtautonom) ---\ndef f_erzwungen(t, y, Omega):\n    # m*x_ddot + c*x_dot + k*x = F0*sin(Omega*t)\n    x_dot  = y[1]\n    x_ddot = None   # TODO: (-k*y[0] - c*y[1] + F0*np.sin(Omega*t)) / m\n    return [x_dot, x_ddot]\n\n# TODO: Simulation für Omega = omega_0 (Resonanz), t_end = 30 s\n# TODO: stationäre Amplitude A = np.max(np.abs(sol.y[0, -n:])) für letztes Drittel\n# TODO: Plot x(t) mit markiertem Transient-Bereich und stationärem Bereich","key":"wPsYOHlyn8"},{"type":"outputs","id":"vFgpDkwbs-hOIZ-cAyTSi","children":[],"key":"UoFdpedkeo"}],"key":"L8d3uaNsEG"},{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"comment","value":" TODO: Prosatext (~80 Wörter):\n     Erklärung Transient vs. stationärer Zustand.\n     Bei Resonanz Omega = omega_0: maximale stationäre Amplitude, Energie-\n     übertrag optimal. Formel für stationäre Amplitude (zur Verifikation):\n     A_stat = F0 / (k * sqrt((1-r^2)^2 + (2*D*r)^2)) mit r = Omega/omega_0.\n     Verweis auf Aufgabe 11.4 (Resonanzkurve als Schleife). ","key":"R9lr38HuXn"},{"type":"admonition","children":[{"type":"admonitionTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mini-Übung","position":{"start":{"line":151,"column":1},"end":{"line":151,"column":1}},"key":"x6svRNIaZL"}],"key":"O6pNkMbVl2"},{"type":"comment","value":" TODO: Mini-Übung (5 min):\n     1. Ist f_erzwungen autonom oder nichtautonom? Woran erkennen Sie das?\n     2. Warum muss t_end für die erzwungene Schwingung länger gewählt werden\n        als für die freie Schwingung?\n     3. Verständnisfrage: Was passiert bei D → 0 und Omega = omega_0 mit der\n        stationären Amplitude? ","key":"NGJ30jwZvv"}],"class":"tip","key":"KJkXFONrPo"}],"key":"lkYYiGB5if"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-code","children":[{"type":"code","lang":"python","executable":true,"value":"# Code-Zelle","key":"XxKUfkVImS"},{"type":"outputs","id":"JmvTZuPj3Z3c5d9-uEp2i","children":[],"key":"lcyabt8CBC"}],"key":"LmLWjyL2k3"},{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"admonition","children":[{"type":"admonitionTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lösung","position":{"start":{"line":165,"column":1},"end":{"line":165,"column":1}},"key":"wwkCeksqZL"}],"key":"kadapNabZS"},{"type":"comment","value":" TODO: Lösung zur Mini-Übung ","key":"RFC6sAgBVI"}],"class":"tip dropdown","key":"dVSrLXNJ1B"}],"key":"NJSZXxHUKS"},{"type":"block","position":{"start":{"line":171,"column":1},"end":{"line":171,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":173,"column":1},"end":{"line":173,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Methodenübersicht Kapitel 10–11","position":{"start":{"line":173,"column":1},"end":{"line":173,"column":1}},"key":"LXtV8jw5oP"}],"identifier":"methoden-bersicht-kapitel-10-11","label":"Methodenübersicht Kapitel 10–11","html_id":"methoden-bersicht-kapitel-10-11","implicit":true,"key":"xFQaLEvsdX"},{"type":"comment","value":" TODO: Unterabschnitt 3 (~8 min)\n     Zusammenfassungstabelle: Wann Euler / solve_ivp, 1 Zustand / 2 Zustände / nichtautonom.\n     Tabelle mit Spalten: Problem | DGL-Typ | Zustandsvektor | f-Signatur | Empfehlung\n\n     Zeilen:\n     - Abkühlung/RC/Zerfall: 1. Ordnung, y=[T], f(t,y)=[...], solve_ivp\n     - Federschwinger: 2. Ordnung autonom, y=[x,v], f(t,y)=[v,...], solve_ivp\n     - Erzwungene Schwingung: 2. Ordnung nichtautonom, y=[x,v], f(t,y) nutzt t, solve_ivp\n     - Einfache Schätzaufgaben: Euler als Lehrbeispiel (sec01/02 Kap. 10)\n\n     Kurzer Ausblick: Was kommt nach DGL? Systeme höherer Ordnung (z.B. 2 gekoppelte\n     Massen), partielle DGLen (FEM). ","key":"GJtbrKim28"},{"type":"admonition","children":[{"type":"admonitionTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Methodenübersicht: DGLen in Kapitel 10 und 11","position":{"start":{"line":188,"column":1},"end":{"line":188,"column":1}},"key":"ivJqF6leBU"}],"key":"O69gDU5hAZ"},{"type":"comment","value":" TODO: Tabelle einfügen:\n| Problem | Zustandsvektor | `y0` | `sol.y` |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Abkühlung, RC-Laden, Zerfall | $y = [T]$ | `[T0]` | `sol.y[0]`: Zustand |\n| Federschwinger (frei) | $y = [x, \\dot{x}]$ | `[x0, v0]` | `sol.y[0]`: Pos., `sol.y[1]`: Geschw. |\n| Gedämpfter Schwinger | $y = [x, \\dot{x}]$ | `[x0, v0]` | wie oben |\n| Erzwungene Schwingung | $y = [x, \\dot{x}]$ | `[x0, v0]` | wie oben, `f` nutzt `t` |\n","key":"w72BufQdbG"}],"class":"note","key":"YJIEFSVRuH"}],"key":"ZW37RJXD34"},{"type":"block","position":{"start":{"line":200,"column":1},"end":{"line":200,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":202,"column":1},"end":{"line":202,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Zusammenfassung und Ausblick","position":{"start":{"line":202,"column":1},"end":{"line":202,"column":1}},"key":"TlfFegpujG"}],"identifier":"zusammenfassung-und-ausblick","label":"Zusammenfassung und Ausblick","html_id":"zusammenfassung-und-ausblick","implicit":true,"key":"f6QFBTFlHf"},{"type":"comment","value":" TODO: Zusammenfassung (~80 Wörter):\n     - Dämpfungszahl D steuert qualitatives Verhalten: schwingend / Grenzfall / kriechend\n     - Erzwungene Schwingung: nichtautonom, stationäre Amplitude aus letztem Zeitdrittel\n     - Resonanz: maximale Amplitude bei Omega ≈ omega_0\n     - Methodenübersicht: solve_ivp mit y0=[x0, v0] funktioniert für alle Fälle\n     - Ausblick auf sec04 (Resonanzkurve numerisch), sec05 (Parameterstudie Fahrzeugfederung) ","key":"frMeStYrJb"}],"key":"Zp2BTagZbj"}],"key":"KShlKeagcX"},"references":{"cite":{"order":[],"data":{}}},"footer":{"navigation":{"prev":{"title":"11.2 Übungen zum Federschwinger","url":"/chapter11-sec02","group":"11. Numerik DGL 2. Ordnung"},"next":{"title":"11.4 Übungen zur gedämpften Schwingung","url":"/chapter11-sec04","group":"11. Numerik DGL 2. Ordnung"}}},"domain":"http://localhost:3000"}